    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Fiacco and McCormick&#x27;s sequential unconstrained minimization replaces \min x^2+y^2 subject to x+y=1 with the unconstrained problems \min x^2+y^2+\mu(x+y-1)^2 for growing \mu. Each penalized minimizer violates the constraint slightly, and the violation shrinks like 1/\mu as the minimizers approach the constrained optimum (0.5, 0.5).">

